From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: run FEX's image-map notification as a syscall callback

NotifyImageMap could deadlock; the syscall-callback guard is now held
across the call, as every other callback does.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-09-24-bootstrap.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
index 77a1c9c..9d53a2f 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/signal_arm64ec.c
@@ -1971,6 +1971,7 @@ static void notify_map_view_of_section( HANDLE handle, void *addr, SIZE_T size,
 void arm64ec_notify_image_map( void *base )
 {
     static unsigned int n_map;
+    BOOL guarded;
 
     /* ml710: must be the intervals-only entry point, NEVER NotifyMapViewOfSection.
      * The latter also drives ImageTracker, which takes FEX's CodeInvalidationMutex
@@ -1980,10 +1981,20 @@ void arm64ec_notify_image_map( void *base )
      * loader lock held. If pNotifyImageMap is absent, do nothing: the syscall path is
      * still authoritative, and a wedge is far worse than a missed registration. */
     if (!base || !pNotifyImageMap) return;
+    /* image-map-guard: hold the syscall-callback guard across the call, as every
+     * other FEX notification does. NotifyImageMap holds FEX's IntervalsLock
+     * exclusively while it allocates, frees and logs; unguarded, a nested
+     * NtFreeVirtualMemory or NtProtectVirtualMemory notifies FEX again and
+     * InvalidateAlignedInterval() waits on that same lock on the same thread,
+     * forever (every child pseudo-process on the rung-4 device run). When the guard
+     * is already set (ml710's stuck-InSyscallCallback case) the call is made as
+     * before, so that fallback is kept. */
+    guarded = enter_syscall_callback();
     n_map++;
     if (n_map <= 64)
         ERR( "[ldr-image] ml710 MAP #%u base=%p peb=%p\n", n_map, base, RtlGetCurrentPeb() );
     pNotifyImageMap( base );
+    if (guarded) leave_syscall_callback();
 }
 
 /* ml709b: UNUSED, deliberately. The loader must not call this -- see the long comment
